# Master Set List (MSL) v3.13 — 140 Node Master Gold Set

**Project Initialization Date:** May 23, 2026

## Project Purpose
The **Master Set List (MSL)** was developed as a high-quality, technically rigorous **audiophile test suite** for evaluating stereo hardware performance.

**Core Goals:**
- Provide repeatable, diagnostic-grade tracks for testing specific aspects of audio reproduction (transient speed, imaging, dynamic headroom, frequency response, phase coherence, etc.).
- Balance technical utility with musical enjoyment.
- Maintain a clean, version-controlled, and well-documented collection that can evolve over time.
- Serve as a consistent benchmark across different listening sessions and hardware configurations.

The set is intentionally curated and maintained with engineering precision (similar to how performance benchmarks are managed in professional systems work).

## Hardware Configurations
Two primary systems are used for evaluation:

| System | Primary Use | Notes |
|--------|-------------|-------|
| **Main Stereo System** | Primary critical listening & testing | Rotel RA-1572 MKII → Sonus Faber Cremona |
| **Tesla Model 3 Highland** | Secondary / mobile reference | High-resolution FLAC playback via Roon + Qobuz on Samsung T7 Shield SSD |

The MSL is primarily used on the main stereo system, with the Tesla system serving as a secondary validation platform.

